item.xCal:description:
Reddacliff Place sculptures will be lit Red to support Go Dotty Day 2026
&nbsp;
Go Dotty Day 2026 - Our nationally recognised "Go Dotty Day" on 2nd October annually raises awareness of Ladybird Care Foundation and the support we provide to bereaved parents. The date, 2nd October coincides with the birthday of Emma Pascoe, daughter of the founders of Ladybird Care Foundation. Emma passed away just before her 18th birthday and is the inspiration for Ladybird Care Foundation, who provides bereavement care to parents who have lost a child (of any age) through our Peer Mentoring program.
&nbsp;
This Light Up is organised by: Ladybird Care Foundation Ltd

