City Hall will be lit Black, Red and Yellow to celebrate German National Day
&nbsp;
German National Day, celebrated on 3 October each year, symbolises the reunification of Germany in 1990 and honours the values of peace, democracy and solidarity that emerged from this historic moment. Through this gesture, the Office of the Honorary Consul of Germany seeks to share the spirit of unity with the Brisbane community, highlight the close friendship between Germany and Australia, and recognise the contributions of German-Australian relations to the city’s cultural and social life but also aligned values in business, innovation and research.
&nbsp;
This Light Up is organised by: The Office of the Honorary Consul of Germany

